menu "Demos"

config FIREWORKS_DEMO
    tristate "Fireworks scheduler stress demo"
    depends on !FLANTERM_CONSOLE
    help
        Draw fireworks on the framebuffer once the kernel is up, with
        one thread per rocket and per particle. Every thread plots its
        pixel, sleeps for a frame and moves on, so a volley keeps a
        few thousand threads sleeping and waking 60 times a second.
        Statistics go to the log every couple of seconds. It runs until
        the machine is turned off, or for fireworks.runtime-seconds=<n>
        from the kernel command line.

        The demo owns the framebuffer, which is why it cannot be
        combined with the framebuffer log console.

endmenu
